; pell_k34.spu - the same loop with K = 34: iteration 34 would need x34, which does not fit 64-bit fields (ISA draft 7.2)
; The SMUL refuses; BR RF takes the overflow branch; the destination keeps its last good value.
; Result: S0 = x33 = (3743165875258953026, 2161117825702177665, 1) preserved, S7 = 1 (stopped by overflow).
; Source reconstructed from the frozen image hardware/tests/psurd_rtl0c/session_v1/B_K34.spui; it assembles byte for byte to that image
; (sha256 1b0f796b16161b5499a2b850572235cb795dafafdf80d869675ef2c4abe15e6f) with --profile programmable-surd.
.profile programmable-surd

        LOADT S1, 2, 1, 1       ; 2 + sqrt3
        SLIK  S0, 1             ; x = 1
        SLIK  S3, 1             ; one
        SLIK  S4, 34            ; remaining count K
        STST  S4
        BR    LT, invalid       ; K < 0
        BR    EQ, done          ; K = 0: no iterations
loop:   SMUL  S0, S0, S1
        BR    RF, overflow      ; refused: S0 still holds the last good x
        SSUB  S4, S4, S3
        STST  S4
        BR    GT, loop
done:   SLIK  S7, 0             ; completed
        HALT
overflow: SLIK S7, 1            ; stopped by overflow refusal
        HALT
invalid: SLIK S7, -1            ; negative count
        HALT
